From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 19:09:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 71/83] web-app: expose safe-link + account-bound QR openers
 for the HTML-email viewer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The HTML-email viewer renders sender HTML in a script-less sandbox, so a
link clicked inside it can't reach React. It relays such links to the app
(runtime.openAppLink), which calls two globals registered here:

- __slothfulOpenLinkSafely(url): http(s) links, run through the existing
  useOpenNonMailtoLinkSafely hook so they get the same tracking-parameter
  stripping a pasted or in-chat link gets. Account-agnostic.
- __slothfulProcessQr(accountId, url): app links (mailto/openpgp4fpr/
  dcaccount/dclogin/i.delta.chat invites) run through processQr bound to
  the account the mail belongs to, passed explicitly — so the link runs
  under that account even if the user switched the app to another one.

Only the web-app runtime ever sets/uses these; upstream/electron never
touch them.
---
 .../src/components/RuntimeAdapter.tsx         | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/frontend/src/components/RuntimeAdapter.tsx b/packages/frontend/src/components/RuntimeAdapter.tsx
index 88876b5..42bcdd0 100644
